  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nOne higher-rank tensor Clifford child cannot replace equal-width, same-direction independent lanes through an arbitrary invertible reciprocal basis change, even with arbitrary dirty padding restored. This package proves the all-size characteristic-zero statement using square trace, dimension and `tr(A) tr(A^3)`, extending the basis choice beyond the prior monomial support argument while keeping independent nonreciprocal adapters outside its scope.\n\nThe direction premise is essential. Two opposite-direction width-f lanes are similar to a phased width-(f+1) child iff f is odd; f divisible by four permits only an unchanged-rank child, and f congruent to two permits none. Three complete rational basis witnesses are supplied. For sixteen uniform rank-one lanes on 32 coordinates, every reciprocal encoding plus a left correction needs `rank(F-I)>=6`; this is a structural lower bound, not a recursive-cost lower bound or attainment claim.\n\nEven with the odd-width encodings free, the inherited volume-linear budget gives `2 A V (f+1)^sigma > 2 A V f^sigma`. This compares available upper-bound expressions, not optimal runtime. No physical decoder, 5% construction-gate success, supplier admission, selected-frontier change or new kappa is claimed. Only `research/clifford-reciprocal-basis-obstruction/` is added.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nBase current main `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`; chooser nonce `5539eb9e61a07a24d746ce2018c34aba`, revision-3 `complex-rank-shape-decoder`, scope `02b31ebd160542c86299/reciprocal-linear-encoding/uniform-and-opposite-directions`. [Discussion1901](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1901) records the claim and completion. TASK.json explicitly records the changed scope from physical synthesis to the prerequisite contract theorem and its exact direction exception.\n\nPR679 supplies the monomial support/volume argument. Ross Richardson's completed source-bound audit at `8a3900c84213fd7603b99beaceaff48f501b4232` is read and credited, not replayed. PR1779 head `1e3128bf642bbaf250b7d6b9639b2bb24b98ce5e` proposes diagonal batches; PR1817 head `ac3a759e874e8e526bc884fc2cb8eb114695b063` verifies retimed original children and leaves their replacement open. This result does not repeat their support counts, scheduling or hosting audits. Exact live kernel and PR679 source blobs/hashes are in SOURCES.json; selected/catalogue pins are historical provenance. Final 13:45\u201313:46 UTC snapshots covered 567 open PRs including drafts and 539 Discussion records with complete pagination. ToikY's parallel [clean-subspace claim](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1901#discussioncomment-18925296) explicitly leaves this full-space result to this work; its clean injective premise is outside our theorem. PR1651's opposite-direction root shears concern another operator. TASK.json records coverage limits; no novelty guarantee is claimed. Main and both named PR heads were rechecked unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/clifford-reciprocal-basis-obstruction\n```\n\nPassed on CPython 3.12.10, Windows 11, standard library only: 28,032 dimension-matched spectral fixtures through f=64, all four phases and both child directions; independent cyclic multiplicities; 2,728 native Gaussian matrix entries checked against separately executed butterflies; three complete rational basis identities; independent Gaussian elimination and four nonmonomial correction-rank probes. Six focused tests cover exact eigenspaces, phase/basis mutations, domain and duplicate-key rejection, actual source/inventory and receipt/type corruption, optimized read-only no-Git export and deterministic regeneration. Registered optimized replay, source/metadata pins, selected-record integrity and staged whitespace checks pass. VALIDATION.json records exact receipt hashes.\n\nThe all-size proof is written mathematics, not kernel verification or independent human review. Full selected cold replay, new physical/compiler/hosting and precision/tape contracts, Lean and hosted CI were not run locally.\n\n## Credit\n\nGreer Guthrie/PR679; Ross Richardson's contract audit; Jose Manuel (@jmbarrancoml) with publishing account Cinna Davis (@1337isnot1337)/PR1779; Josie Elliston/PR1817; icekylinx, DreamingOfClouds and the original kernel/volume lineage; Sagar Thakrar/PR1012, Douglas Colkitt, Rohan Arun, Jeremy Kothe, Hao Yan and retained selected contributors. Arham Tahir/PR1605 supplies the preceding integer price screen. No priority claim for trace invariants, Walsh diagonalization or rank perturbation inequalities.\n\nPrepared by Arham Tahir with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in research, proof, code, checks and writing. No subagents. Apache-2.0; existing sources/notices remain intact.\n\n## Open next questions\n\nThe README/TASK give two bounded continuations: an independently priced nonreciprocal adapter, or a real opposite-direction boundary with a proved changed volume contract. Arbitrary independent maps can force an invertible target, but legal inexpensive adapters remain missing. The inherited joined-array tariff already rejects the displayed mixed identity with conversions free.\n",
